userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The sine of an angle is the height (y-coordinate) of the corresponding point on the unit circle, so the graph of y = sin(x) is a running record of that height as the angle sweeps around the circle.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The sine curve isn't a separate object from the circle — it is the circle point's height plotted against the angle, so every feature of the graph (the rise to 1, the fall, the negative dip) is just where the point sits vertically on the circle.
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

